{"flows":{"ns":{"scope":"Representative silicon nanosheet nFET fabrication using a replacement metal gate; selected isolation scheme (full bottom dielectric isolation) and illustrative materials. Not a verified foundry recipe.","refs":["R13"],"views":{"cut":{"n":"Gate cutaway","s":"through the gate centre, at an angle","az":1.02,"el":0.34,"r":255,"tgt":[0,44,0],"clip":[0,null,null]},"cutb":{"n":"Channel cutaway","s":"along the channel, at an angle","az":-0.62,"el":0.3,"r":225,"tgt":[0,44,0],"clip":[null,null,0]}},"steps":[{"id":"substrate","title":"Silicon substrate","body":"A crystalline silicon wafer, cleaned and prepared for epitaxy. The flow must also stop current leaking through the silicon beneath the channels: this model uses full bottom dielectric isolation (BDI) for that; a doped punch-through stopper is another published approach.","view":"iso","parts":[{"id":"wafer","name":"Si substrate (unpatterned)","material":"silicon","group":"Substrate & isolation","boxes":[[0.0,-13.0,0.0,96.0,26.0,84.0]],"explode":[0,-1.2,0]}]},{"id":"superlattice","title":"Si/SiGe multilayer epitaxy","body":"Alternating SiGe and Si layers are grown as one solid crystalline stack. The Si layers become the nanosheets; the SiGe occupies the future gate spaces and is removed from the gate region later. The bottom SiGe, richer in Ge, belongs to the chosen isolation scheme: it can be etched selectively against the other SiGe layers.","view":"iso","parts":[{"id":"wafer","name":"Si substrate (unpatterned)","material":"silicon","group":"Substrate & isolation","boxes":[[0.0,-13.0,0.0,96.0,26.0,84.0]],"explode":[0,-1.2,0]},{"id":"bsige","name":"SiGe, high Ge · sacrificial bottom layer","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,5.0,0.0,73.0,10.0,84.0]],"explode":[0,-0.6,0]},{"id":"sige1","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 1","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,16.0,0.0,73.0,12.0,84.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige2","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 2","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,0.0,73.0,16.0,84.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige3","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 3","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,56.0,0.0,73.0,16.0,84.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si1","name":"Si · future nanosheet 1","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,24.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,84.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si2","name":"Si · future nanosheet 2","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,45.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,84.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si3","name":"Si · future nanosheet 3","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,66.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,84.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]}]},{"id":"pattern","title":"Stack patterning and STI","body":"Lithography and etch cut the multilayer into narrow stacks, and on into the substrate as a short sub-fin; the mask sets the sheet width. Trench oxide is deposited, planarised and recessed: shallow trench isolation (STI) separates neighbouring devices sideways. Here it is recessed to the bottom of the high-Ge layer, leaving that layer's sidewalls open for its later removal. How the stack pattern is made depends on the layer, pitch and process: EUV single exposure allows different sheet widths, and dense arrays can also use spacer-based pitch splitting (SADP/SAQP); an example is planned for the FinFET flow.","view":"iso","parts":[{"id":"bsige","name":"SiGe, high Ge · sacrificial bottom layer","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,5.0,0.0,73.0,10.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,-0.6,0]},{"id":"sige1","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 1","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,16.0,0.0,73.0,12.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige2","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 2","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,0.0,73.0,16.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige3","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 3","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,56.0,0.0,73.0,16.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si1","name":"Si · future nanosheet 1","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,24.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si2","name":"Si · future nanosheet 2","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,45.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si3","name":"Si · future nanosheet 3","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,66.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},"substrate","sti"]},{"id":"dummy","title":"Dummy gate stack","body":"A thin sacrificial oxide, a polysilicon placeholder gate and a nitride hard mask are deposited and patterned across the stack. The dummy gate fixes where the gate goes and its length; the real high-κ/metal gate replaces it near the end (replacement metal gate).","view":"iso","parts":[{"id":"bsige","name":"SiGe, high Ge · sacrificial bottom layer","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,5.0,0.0,73.0,10.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,-0.6,0]},{"id":"sige1","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 1","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,16.0,0.0,73.0,12.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige2","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 2","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,0.0,73.0,16.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige3","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 3","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,56.0,0.0,73.0,16.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si1","name":"Si · future nanosheet 1","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,24.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si2","name":"Si · future nanosheet 2","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,45.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si3","name":"Si · future nanosheet 3","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,66.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},"substrate","sti",{"id":"dox","name":"Dummy-gate oxide (sacrificial)","material":"sio2","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,-15.5,15.0,70.0,1.0],[0.0,69.5,0.5,15.0,1.0,31.0],[0.0,34.5,15.5,15.0,69.0,1.0]],"explode":[0,0.6,0]},{"id":"dummy","name":"Dummy gate · polysilicon","material":"poly","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,42.0,-21.0,15.0,84.0,10.0],[0.0,77.0,5.0,15.0,14.0,42.0],[0.0,35.0,21.0,15.0,70.0,10.0]],"explode":[0,1.0,0]},{"id":"hardmask","name":"SiN hard mask","material":"si3n4","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,87.0,0.0,15.0,6.0,52.0]],"explode":[0,1.4,0]}]},{"id":"bottom","title":"Bottom-layer removal","body":"Where the stack is not covered by the dummy gate, its sidewalls are exposed (any covering liner is cleared first), including the high-Ge bottom layer's, which the STI recess left open. A selective etch removes that layer, working in from the exposed sides and on underneath the dummy gate, which holds the stack up over the open cavity. This follows one published early-BDI route [R13].","view":"cutb","parts":[{"id":"sige1","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 1","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,16.0,0.0,73.0,12.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige2","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 2","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,0.0,73.0,16.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige3","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 3","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,56.0,0.0,73.0,16.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si1","name":"Si · future nanosheet 1","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,24.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si2","name":"Si · future nanosheet 2","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,45.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si3","name":"Si · future nanosheet 3","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,66.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},"substrate","sti",{"id":"dox","name":"Dummy-gate oxide (sacrificial)","material":"sio2","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,-15.5,15.0,70.0,1.0],[0.0,69.5,0.5,15.0,1.0,31.0],[0.0,34.5,15.5,15.0,69.0,1.0]],"explode":[0,0.6,0]},{"id":"dummy","name":"Dummy gate · polysilicon","material":"poly","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,42.0,-21.0,15.0,84.0,10.0],[0.0,77.0,5.0,15.0,14.0,42.0],[0.0,35.0,21.0,15.0,70.0,10.0]],"explode":[0,1.0,0]},{"id":"hardmask","name":"SiN hard mask","material":"si3n4","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,87.0,0.0,15.0,6.0,52.0]],"explode":[0,1.4,0]}]},{"id":"spacers","title":"Spacer dielectric fill and etch-back","body":"A conformal spacer dielectric is deposited: it fills the cavity under the stack and coats everything else. Etch-back then clears it from the top and sides, leaving the outer spacers on the dummy-gate sidewalls and the bottom dielectric isolation (BDI) under the whole stack [R13]. In that route one dielectric forms both (SiOC, SiCN, SiOCN and SiBCN are its examples); the oxide BDI and nitride spacers here are illustrative substitutes.","view":"cutb","parts":[{"id":"sige1","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 1","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,16.0,0.0,73.0,12.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige2","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 2","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,0.0,73.0,16.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige3","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 3","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,56.0,0.0,73.0,16.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si1","name":"Si · future nanosheet 1","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,24.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si2","name":"Si · future nanosheet 2","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,45.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"si3","name":"Si · future nanosheet 3","material":"silicon","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,66.5,0.0,73.0,5.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},"substrate","sti",{"id":"dox","name":"Dummy-gate oxide (sacrificial)","material":"sio2","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,-15.5,15.0,70.0,1.0],[0.0,69.5,0.5,15.0,1.0,31.0],[0.0,34.5,15.5,15.0,69.0,1.0]],"explode":[0,0.6,0]},{"id":"dummy","name":"Dummy gate · polysilicon","material":"poly","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,42.0,-21.0,15.0,84.0,10.0],[0.0,77.0,5.0,15.0,14.0,42.0],[0.0,35.0,21.0,15.0,70.0,10.0]],"explode":[0,1.0,0]},{"id":"hardmask","name":"SiN hard mask","material":"si3n4","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,87.0,0.0,15.0,6.0,52.0]],"explode":[0,1.4,0]},"bdi",{"id":"spo_source","name":"Si₃N₄ gate spacer · source side","material":"si3n4","group":"Spacers","boxes":[[-11.0,45.0,-20.5,7.0,90.0,11.0],[-11.0,79.5,5.5,7.0,21.0,41.0],[-11.0,34.5,20.5,7.0,69.0,11.0]],"explode":[-1.3,0,0]},{"id":"spo_drain","name":"Si₃N₄ gate spacer · drain side","material":"si3n4","group":"Spacers","boxes":[[11.0,45.0,-20.5,7.0,90.0,11.0],[11.0,79.5,5.5,7.0,21.0,41.0],[11.0,34.5,20.5,7.0,69.0,11.0]],"explode":[1.3,0,0]}]},{"id":"recess","title":"Source/drain recess","body":"The stack outside the gate and spacers is etched away, stopping on the bottom isolation, which stays under the future source and drain. The ends of every Si and SiGe layer are now exposed at the recess walls.","view":"iso","parts":["substrate","sti",{"id":"dox","name":"Dummy-gate oxide (sacrificial)","material":"sio2","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,-15.5,15.0,70.0,1.0],[0.0,69.5,0.5,15.0,1.0,31.0],[0.0,34.5,15.5,15.0,69.0,1.0]],"explode":[0,0.6,0]},{"id":"dummy","name":"Dummy gate · polysilicon","material":"poly","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,42.0,-21.0,15.0,84.0,10.0],[0.0,77.0,5.0,15.0,14.0,42.0],[0.0,35.0,21.0,15.0,70.0,10.0]],"explode":[0,1.0,0]},{"id":"hardmask","name":"SiN hard mask","material":"si3n4","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,87.0,0.0,15.0,6.0,52.0]],"explode":[0,1.4,0]},"bdi",{"id":"spo_source","name":"Si₃N₄ gate spacer · source side","material":"si3n4","group":"Spacers","boxes":[[-11.0,45.0,-20.5,7.0,90.0,11.0],[-11.0,79.5,5.5,7.0,21.0,41.0],[-11.0,34.5,20.5,7.0,69.0,11.0]],"explode":[-1.3,0,0]},{"id":"spo_drain","name":"Si₃N₄ gate spacer · drain side","material":"si3n4","