anneal","body":"After a surface clean, doped silicon (Si:P for this nFET; B-doped SiGe is typical for pFETs) grows from the exposed Si sheet ends. The oxide below is not a crystal seed, so growth starts at the sheets and merges into one shared source on one side and one shared drain on the other, joining the sheet ends. The activation anneal that follows needs no separate step in this model, but it does change the device: dopant activation and diffusion shape the junction profile.","view":"iso","parts":["substrate","sti",{"id":"dox","name":"Dummy-gate oxide (sacrificial)","material":"sio2","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,-15.5,15.0,70.0,1.0],[0.0,69.5,0.5,15.0,1.0,31.0],[0.0,34.5,15.5,15.0,69.0,1.0]],"explode":[0,0.6,0]},{"id":"dummy","name":"Dummy gate · polysilicon","material":"poly","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,42.0,-21.0,15.0,84.0,10.0],[0.0,77.0,5.0,15.0,14.0,42.0],[0.0,35.0,21.0,15.0,70.0,10.0]],"explode":[0,1.0,0]},{"id":"hardmask","name":"SiN hard mask","material":"si3n4","group":"Dummy gate","boxes":[[0.0,87.0,0.0,15.0,6.0,52.0]],"explode":[0,1.4,0]},"bdi",{"id":"sige1","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 1","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,16.0,0.0,15.0,12.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige2","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 2","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,35.0,0.0,15.0,16.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},{"id":"sige3","name":"SiGe · sacrificial layer 3","material":"sige","group":"Superlattice","boxes":[[0.0,56.0,0.0,15.0,16.0,30.0]],"explode":[0,0,0]},"sheet1","sheet2","sheet3","spacer_source","spacer_drain","epi_source","epi_drain"]},{"id":"ild","title":"ILD fill and planarisation","body":"Interlayer dielectric is deposited over everything and polished flat (CMP), stopping on the hard mask. The source and drain are now buried; hide the ILD in Layers to see them.","view":"iso","parts":["substrate","sti",{"id":"dox","name":"Dummy-gate oxide (sacrificial)","material":"sio2","group":"Dummy gate","box